course: dictionary
lesson: 7111
title: Pectin and the word that sets things
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Pectin is a noun, and it is a thing you can find in fruit. It is a natural substance in fruits, especially apples and lemons, and it makes jam and jelly set, which means go thick and firm. If you have ever seen runny jam turn into a firm spread, pectin is often the reason.
explain: You do not need to know the word before you read it. Look at the clues around it. «Gummy sweets are made by squirting hot syrup with gelatine or pectin into shapes.» The sentence puts pectin next to gelatine, and both are used to make the sweets firm. So pectin must be something that helps a mixture set.
explain: Context also tells you where pectin comes from. In the sentence about gummy sweets, it is a powder you can use again after it is sieved and dried. In jam, it is found naturally in fruit. Ask yourself: what job is this word doing in the sentence? Then check your meaning by putting it in place of the word.
fact: Pectin is a natural substance found in fruits, especially apples and lemons.
fact: Pectin makes jam and jelly set, which means go thick and firm.
fact: Some fruits, like strawberries, have little pectin, so cooks add pectin or lemon juice.
fact: Pectin is a kind of fibre, and fibre is healthy to eat.
fact: In «gummy sweets», pectin can be used instead of gelatine to help the sweets set.
exercise: «Pectin is found in apples and lemons.» What is pectin? | A type of fruit juice | *A natural substance in fruit that makes jam set | A kind of hot syrup | A sweet made in trays of cornflour
exercise: Mia's strawberry jam stayed runny. Why might she need to add pectin or lemon juice? | *Strawberries have little pectin | Lemon juice makes jam melt | Strawberries have too much pectin, so the jam is too thick | Strawberries are made of sugar only
exercise: «Gummy sweets are made by squirting hot syrup with gelatine or pectin into shapes.» In this sentence, what is pectin most like? | A tray that holds the sweets | *Gelatine, another thing that helps the sweets set | Cornflour, the powder in the trays | Hot syrup, poured into the shapes
test: Which fruits are named in the dictionary as having a lot of pectin? | Bananas and grapes | *Apples and lemons | Melons and plums | Carrots and peas
test: «Strawberries have little pectin, so people add pectin or lemon juice.» What does this tell you about pectin? | It is a sweet you eat on its own | It is a sugar that makes fruit taste sweet | It is the water inside a fruit | *It is a natural substance that helps jam set, and some fruits need extra
exam: Why is pectin a healthy thing to eat? | It is a vitamin that stops all colds | *It is a kind of fibre | It is a sugar that gives you energy only | It is a fizzy drink in jam
